# XView-on-Qt (thin shim)

XView is implemented the same way Motif is: a public C API over Qt widgets,
not by compiling the Sun sources. This is a **source-level subset**, not the
Sun ABI. Attribute numbers and package ids are defined in
[include/xview/xview.h](../../include/xview/xview.h).

## Packages

| Package | Qt |
| --- | --- |
| FRAME | QMainWindow |
| PANEL | QWidget + QVBoxLayout |
| PANEL_BUTTON | QPushButton |
| PANEL_MESSAGE | QLabel |
| PANEL_TEXT | QLineEdit |
| PANEL_SLIDER | QSlider |
| CANVAS | QWidget; `CANVAS_REPAINT_PROC` paints with QPainter |
| MENU / MENUITEM | QMenu / QAction |
| SCROLLBAR | QScrollBar |
| `xv_notice` | QMessageBox |
| `xv_main_loop` | `QApplication::exec` |

## libolgx

[include/olgx/olgx.h](../../include/olgx/olgx.h) and [olgx.cpp](olgx.cpp).
Boxes, buttons, choice marks, text and scrollbars are drawn with QPainter
using the OPEN LOOK light/dark bevel. During a canvas repaint the calls
paint into that canvas; otherwise they paint an offscreen image.

## Build

```bash
cmake -B build && cmake --build build --target xview-hello
./build/xview-hello
```

`MQ_BUILD_XVIEW=OFF` skips the library. Real XView clients will not link
until the attribute set and package list grow toward the Sun headers.
